course: dictionary
lesson: 1846
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Cockle is a shellfish, a small light boat, and part of a happy feeling in an idiom. Context, the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «There is a skittle-alley, and a little pond with gold-fish, a cockle-shell border.» The clues are pond, gold-fish and border, which are all things in a garden. So cockle-shell must mean a shell, not a boat. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: An idiom is a set phrase whose meaning is not the same as its real words. «It warms the cockles of my heart» has no real warm cockles in it. The clues are warms and heart, so it means the thing makes you feel happy and loved.
fact: Cockle (noun) means a small edible shellfish with two ribbed, heart-shaped shells, found in sand on beaches.
fact: Cockle can also mean a small light boat, also called a cockleshell.
fact: «It warms the cockles of my heart» is an idiom that means it makes me feel happy and loved.
fact: The Irish song «Molly Malone» has the words «cockles and mussels, alive, alive-o».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «There is a cockle-shell border around the pond.» What is a cockle-shell here? | A kind of grass | A pile of sand | *A shell | A small light boat
exercise: Grandma says, «It warms the cockles of my heart» when you give her a hug. What does it mean? | Cockles are cooking in her heart | She feels very cold | Someone has stung her heart | *It makes her feel happy and loved
exercise: Where do cockles live? | Up in the sky | On the moon | In a desert | *Buried in wet sand on beaches
test: «The cockle drifted out to sea, rocking gently on the waves.» What is a cockle in this sentence? | *A small light boat | A feeling of joy | Something you eat for tea | A bird that sings
test: What does the idiom «warms the cockles of my heart» tell you? | *Feeling happy and loved | Feeling hungry | Feeling a sharp pain | Feeling cold after swimming
exam: In the song «cockles and mussels, alive, alive-o», which clue best shows that cockles are food from the sea? | Cockles are a kind of bird | The song is about a boat race | Alive, alive-o is a dance | *Mussels, another shellfish, appear beside them
